[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]external_artifact_ingestion.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/external_artifact_ingestion.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-jd[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-jd/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]external_ref bead identity field[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]bead_ref[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead_ref: add the nullable, partially-unique external_ref column to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-core bead schema and thread it through wire, jsonl, events, read, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mutation, CLI, history, and search plus the Python mirrors; add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project-qualified external ref normalizer and widen bug_links to task [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]beads through it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pull-request provider seam[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]pr_seam[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pr_seam: add PullRequestWire, vcs_list_pull_requests, and split [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]list/read/mutate capability probes to the VCS provider boundary, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]implement them in sase-github over gh pr list, extend the in-memory [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fake, and add provider_id to IssueWire.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]PR_ORIGIN field, SASE_PATCH stamp, and the external-Patch [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]safety exclusion[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]pr_origin[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pr_origin: add the tri-state PR_ORIGIN Patch field across parser, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]storage, section order, and the four ACE styling surfaces; stamp [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SASE_PATCH in append_pr_tags; and structurally exclude external Patches [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from AXE work before any importer can create one.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]external_issue_mirror chop[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]issue_mirror[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bead_ref[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]issue_mirror: add the per-project builtin chop that diffs the tracker [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]against beads on external_ref and creates unsized open task beads, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]watermarks, a resumable backfill, per-pass budgets, backoff, a daily [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repair scan, a dry run, and a doctor check for detached tracker auth.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]external_pr_mirror chop and the two-file Patch importer[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]pr_mirror[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pr_seam, pr_origin[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pr_mirror: add the per-project builtin chop that adopts unowned remote [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PRs as Patches, built on a new importer that locks the active and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]archive ProjectSpec files together and writes merged and closed PRs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]straight into the archive.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]External-issue presentation and actions in the Beads pane[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]bead_bug_ui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bead_ref[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead_bug_ui: give Beads the external-issue chip, drift badge, detail [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section, capability-gated migrated actions, and bug filter tokens [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]additively, while the Bugs sub-tab is still present, backed by one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bounded per-project cache refresh.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]PR badge and origin chip on Patch rows and detail[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]patch_pr_ui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pr_origin[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]patch_pr_ui: render the PR badge and the origin chip as two independent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]signals on Patch rows and in the detail panel, add the origin query [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]property, and add the mark-origin/adopt operation that clears unknown [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]records.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retire Bugs, rename PRs to Patches, reorder the Artifacts [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]sub-tabs[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]tabs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bead_bug_ui, issue_mirror[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tabs: collapse the Artifacts sub-tabs to Stitches, Patches, Beads, Files[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]by deleting the Bugs pane and renaming the prs identifier to patches, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]keeping deprecated action aliases, and regenerating every affected text [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and PNG golden.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-jd","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-jd.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-jd.1"},"source_run_id":"run-8519867c74763b0e9365aedcd021c9b6","started_at":"2026-08-10T23:17:45.633779+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"30c4af9033875ec2e4b7a83223a70e394fc9b2177e35eae112857a6b6f8997eb","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-jd.8/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"d